claude-flightdeck, by Stephen Casella: https://github.com/scasella/claude-flightdeck

Ideas taken: a pane of panels fed by the session's own events (vitals with a context gauge and compaction marks, a permission gate with
one cell per tool check settled by the tool call, subagent cards and swimlanes, a turn receipt, a session log), connectors and clocks
drawn as surface modules that redraw only themselves and move only while work flows, the layout names (auto, compact, wide, mini), the
option names layout, motion, panels, maxCards, openOnStart and statusLine, and a list of credential patterns to mask.

Code: the Deck (the second pane) and the Black Box card were first written with that project open beside them. Some lines in these files
are still the same as, or close to, lines of claude-flightdeck 0.3.2: hooks/elapsed.tsx, hooks/rail.tsx, hooks/deckfmt.ts,
hooks/agentcards.ts, hooks/gate.ts, hooks/mask.ts, hooks/sessionlog.ts, hooks/deckconfig.ts and parts of hooks/deckview.ts. Treat those
files as adapted from it. The colours, the drawings and every other file are Cockpit's own.

